From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:06:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: composer options -- effort on the right, options
 button last, switches

Three changes to the row under the composer and the Agent Options
menu, as the operator laid them out on 2026-11-20.

Effort moves right. Upstream's df1ba676 split the config options into
response controls on the left (speed and effort) and the rest on the
right. Effort now follows the model it depends on: the right-hand row
reads context ring, mode, model, effort, options button, send. Speed
stays a response control on the left; Claude Agent (Plus) sends none
there -- its Fast mode is a model_config boolean, so it lives in the
menu -- and the left row (add context, preview, follow, voice) is
unchanged. split_config_options orders the toolbar Speed, Mode, Model,
ThoughtLevel, and only Speed is a response control.

Effort keeps its compact trigger (thinking_effort_trigger), which
upstream tied to being a response control; it is now tied to the
ThoughtLevel category, and its picker opens leftwards (BottomRight),
as the model's does, since it no longer sits at the row's left end.

The options button closes the row. ConfigOptionsView rendered it
before the selectors; it now comes after them, so it sits after effort
and before Send.

On/off options are switches. Plus offers three in the menu: Fast mode
and Ultracode as booleans, and Thinking as a select whose values are
"on" and "off" (thinking-option.ts; it stays a select even for a
client that takes booleans, and offers "on" alone for a model that
always thinks). Upstream drew a boolean as a check-marked entry with
its description in a side panel, and that select as a submenu opening
a picker of its own -- a second popover to flip one setting. Every
on/off option is now one row: the name, with the description as its
tooltip, and a ui::Switch. A click anywhere on the row, the switch
included, flips it; the switch has no handler of its own, or one click
would flip it twice. An "on"-only select draws a disabled switch and a
muted name. The new module config_options/switch_row.rs decides what
is a switch (switch_state), what flips it (flipped_value) and draws
the row; selects with other values stay submenus.

The menu stays open. It is built with ContextMenu::build_persistent,
so a click on a row rebuilds it instead of dismissing it, and
rebuild_selectors -- which runs on every config update and used to
close the menu -- now redraws it in place while it holds the focus,
so the switch shows the agent's answer where it was clicked. The menu
still closes when it has nothing left to show, or when a submenu's
picker holds the focus, as before. Every switch flips the option for
this session only, as booleans already did (0059); Shift sets no
default.

Tests (config_options::tests): on_off_options_are_switches_that_keep_
the_menu_open (new) -- Thinking is no submenu, its row sends "on", the
menu stays focused after the click and after the agent's update, and
the Ultracode row sends a boolean, with no default saved;
effort_is_not_a_response_control (new). Upstream's composer_uses_the_
first_matching_option_for_each_toolbar_control now expects fast-mode,
mode, model, effort, and overflow_options_stay_editable_after_a_
config_update clicks the boolean's switch row and checks the menu
stayed open instead of reopening it, and after the submenu's choice it
checks the menu is still open and focused rather than clicking it open
again (which would now close it). switch_row::tests cover the
shapes: a boolean, an on/off select, an "on"-only select, and selects
that stay submenus.
